Finally! After who knows how many attempts at Wiz-Hum-Mal-Neu, I
finally ascended one after a few weeks of RL time. (Yes, I was adamant
that it has to be Wiz-Hum-Mal-Neu, no matter what, even though I had
no particular reason for this.)

(Unrelated question: how do you see the high score list without having
to create a throwaway character and escaping the dungeon?)

I actually managed to do it genoless (my first time!), although it was
mostly a consequence of circumstances rather than an active decision
from the beginning.  Throughout the game I never found a ?oGeno, and
found that with Magicbane, cloak of MR, SDSM, teleportitis/TC, liches
were manageable.  Mind flayers weren't too bad either once I mastered
cancellation and FoD and can dispatch them quickly. Rust monsters
never bothered me since I stuck with pure spellcasting armor, and
disenchanters I cancelled and dispatched at a distance. It does take
careful play, but quite doable, so I never bothered to wish for/write
a ?oGeno myself.

Anyway, this was a very long game, and I'm recalling this from memory
(I had given up taking notes several YASD's ago) so some things are a
bit unclear. It started out as a not-so-serious game ("Buta" is a
perjorative meaning "blind" btw), with =oPM, force bolt and MM. MM was
good advantage in the early game. Anyway, the earliest part of the
game involved fooling around with polymorphing; I stowed away my
starting equipment in a box and put on the =oPM and waited until I
turned into a powerful monster, then I dived down the dungeon killing
things until I turned back to human form, then I fled back upstairs.
Found Mines early on around Dlvl:2 or Dlvl:3. and flew in as a dragon,
killing stuff. Turned into a fire ant at one point and scuttled
downstairs setting monsters on fire. Got to about Exp:3 or 4 this way,
before I decided to take things a bit more seriously.

I started training the cat up to be a large cat, and pushed boulders
around until St:14 or so. Acquired a large collection of daggers and
did target practice in the Mines. Found a leash and magic whistle
somewhere along the line, and took pet to Minetown and robbed the
shops, but altar was non-coaligned so could only BCU stuff. Found 2
crystal balls in the Mines, one in a shop, but ended up never using
them. It was the night theme version of Minetown, and I didn't find
the down stairs at first, so went back to main dungeon with a pickaxe
to find vaults. Broke through a few vaults, found the Oracle where I
got caught in a magic trap and had a big battle with nasty monsters.
This made me decide not to go further until I bought some protection.
So I collected vault cash and headed to Minetown, and got intrinsic
AC:6.

At some point, I decided to go look for Sokoban; so slowly descended
past Oracle with pet. Managed to clear out Sokoban slowly. Pet almost
got killed at zoo, but I managed to clear it out, got AoR. Got
confident at this progress, so went back to Minetown and looked for
down stairs.

Started to descend slowly past Minetown with pet.  However, lost pet
in a PM trap: pet got polymorphed into a pony (low level) while I
fought some tough monsters; pet got killed in the aftermath. Retreated
back to Minetown.  Went back to main dungeon and tried to find more
cash for protection.  Eventually, didn't get anything beyond AC 5, not
enough cash. So realized I need to find a coaligned altar or convert
one. Had to go several levels beyond Sokoban before found first altar;
failed to convert altar several times, so gave up. Decided that I
needed more alignment increase; so went back to the Mines and tried to
hit Mine bottom. Slowly managed to get to bottom, got the gems. At
this point, I got too much stuff so found a chest in a gnome's home in
Minetown and stored stuff there (at first I just left the stuff in the
temple but then soldiers started robbing the stash). Somewhere around
this time, I got essential invis and see invis from stalkers, so I had
to play with mummy wrappings to visit shops. Went back to main dungeon
to try to convert altars.

Finally, converted altar at around Dlvl:11 or so. So began to sac. Got
a few spellbooks. This is probably the longest part of the game. Moved
the stash from Minetown to new altar, got teleport control from eating
tengus, so decided to eat a nymph to get teleportitis. Did more
boulder-pushing until St:17. Descended main dungeon very slowly. Got
AC reduced to 1 from sac'ing and praying. Found large room just below
altar.  Fort Ludios just below that. Another altar was below Fort
Ludios but didn't go that far at the time.

Found silver dragon scales in Fort Ludios and started wearing them.
(Was wearing +1 leather armor at this point.) Pushed boulder into moat
to cross; cleared out fort, got the gems. Went with lots of cash to
Minetown to buy more protection, but didn't get any 'cos already at
AC:1 (sighhh...). I guess the chances for this are really low. Anyway,
eventually found some ?oEA, and made SDSM. Found the Quest, and
cleared it. Nemesis was a joke... I used ?oEarth to block the up
stairs, and a few MM's later he was history. So I got the Eye and wore
it ever since.

At some point, came across beehive and got St:18/01 or thereabouts.
Started descending more. Got lots of spellbooks from sac'ing, also
from chests and boxes. Eventually got very good AC (about -20 or so).
Found a BoH somewhere (forgot exactly where). Descended slowly to
about level 20 or so, collecting stuff. Then, the most stupid mistake:
I had collected a large number of pots, ready for alchemy and making
holy water, so the BoH was quite heavy. I was just about to return to
the altar stash when I found a bag of tricks, but it made me burdened.
But I want to keep it for sac'ing... "Oh I know, stick it in the BoH
with the other heavy stuff." Poof. BoH vanished. The stupid thing was,
I didn't even notice, except that I was no longer burdened, as I
hoped.  (Didn't realize it was 'cos the bag was gone!) Didn't even
realize until I looted the next chest, and was about to stow away the
stuff, when ...  wait a sec, where's the bag gone??! Took me a while
to remember I tried putting the BoT into it. D'oh. I lost a LOT of
stuff in this accident... including practically all the important
spellbooks (including FoD!), since only the "useless" spellbooks were
left at the stash, and all my gems. (That'll teach me to carry them
around for no reason.) Lost at least a few artifact weapons as well,
plus a good number of important scrolls, tools, etc.. There was a +4
mummy wrapping I used for shopkeeper-pacifying (and sac-monster
luring) purposes, and a blessed tinning kit I'd been using to beef up
on giant corpses. I had collected quite a number of ?oEW, and had made
a collection of 50 rustproof +7 daggers for dispensible use in
Gehennom.  Of these, 40 were in the bag.  Ouchie. There goes the
dispensible idea.  Worst of all, the next level was Medusa, with the
Titan.  Just as I was gonna FoD the Titan, I forgot the spell, and the
spellbook's already gone.  Grrr.

So I went back to the altar stash, and wondered what to do. Finally
decided to do something with my collection of unicorn horns and the
last few charges on a /oPM. Guess what, got lucky, and got a magic
marker on first zap.  Tried it a few more times but didn't turn up
anything else useful. Also wasted a b?oCharging on the magic marker
(and learned the hard way that they can only be recharged once).
Anyway, I blanked a spellbook and rewrote +oFoD, relearned it, and
FoDded the Titan on Medusa.  Only to find that it had gotten magic
resistance, so FoD didn't work.  (Sigh...) Anyway, I MM'd it to death
before it could do much more. Then I realized that I had lost my
levboots (either that or =oLev) in the BoH accident, so I couldn't
cross the water.

So began a second long stage of the game in the main dungeon, just
wandering about and collecting stuff and sac'ing. Got magic mapping
from praying at some point.  Went back to Ludios and collected all the
leather gloves the soldiers dropped, and Id'd them. This was before I
got +oId from sac'ing, so it was a painstaking process of BUC'ing them
on the altar below the Ludios level and trying them on one by one.
This effort paid off. I found a pair of +4 leather gloves which I wore
until ascension. (I had used up the magic marker from the polypile,
which was already "recharged" once when I got it from the polypile, so
I was on a shortage of ?oEM, having just fireproofed my cloak of MR.)
Did the same for jackboots, although there weren't as many around so I
only managed to find a blessed +1 pair. Anyway, I didn't find a BoH
again, so I moved some of the essential parts of the stash to an altar
just 2 levels above Medusa and started preparing to enter the castle.
Finally, I found a =oLev (forgot exactly where, though), so I headed
down to Medusa.

Medusa was easy, but harder than my previous games. Somehow SDSM
doesn't seem to reflect her gaze? (Or was that 'cos I was
blindfolded?) Anyway, she went down in a couple o' MMs. Found
reflection shield on Perseus' statue, but it hindered spellcasting so
I gave up.

Castle was directly below Medusa, and was lots of fun. I had knock and
wizard lock handy, and all it took was just standing a distance away
from the drawbridge, and opening it to let out a few monsters, then
closing it to kill them. "The drawbridge closes! The soldier falls
into the water. You killed the soldier! The demilich disappears behind
the portcullis! You hear smashing and crushing." Did this for most of
the soldiers, liches, and demiliches. Let out a few giants for eating
purposes. :-) I think there was a mindflayer or two, that I made sure
got crushed by the portcullis. >:-) Worked my way into the castle, and
started to get all loaded up from all the goodies therein. For
safety's sake, I deposited some of the loot in a chest and headed for
the WoW - to wish for a blessed greased BoH, of course. :-) I had
found an oilskin sack previously, which I was using, so it became my
backup bag for holding wands (I've come to be really paranoid about
the integrity of my BoH). Saved the other two wishes for later.
Cleared out the castle, but didn't feel ready enough for Gehennom yet,
so went back to the altar stash.

Moved my main stash down to Dlvl:26, the nearest altar to Medusa.
There were actually quite a number of (non-coaligned) temples in the
main dungeon, but I didn't do much with them, felt it was too risky to
attempt converting them. Anyway, thus began another long stretch of
the game, mostly sac'ing, and collecting stuff, trying to decide what
I need for the ascension run. Spent quite some time to collect potions
for making holy/unholy water, doing alchemy to make healing pots, etc.
Managed to get my HP to 300+ and Pw to 300+ or so. Got lots more
spellbooks from sac'ing, including Id, create monster, charm monster,
etc.. Gained several levels from wraiths. Enhanced spellcasting to
expert in attack, divination, and matter (cancellation turned out very
useful against MF's and MMF's), and basic in enchantment and clerical
(the clerical was from continual casting of create monster for sac'ing
:-P). Never bothered to advance quarterstaff skills after reading
about being unable to cast spells or take stuff out of bags from
wielding a cursed quarterstaff; I had just been surviving on MM and
daggers. At some point, I (finally) got Magicbane from sac'ing. Played
around with charm monster, got an owlbear and a carnivorous ape as
pets (called Boohyoo and Feedme, respectively) to rob the shop on
Dlvl:26, but found they didn't last very long with the high-level
monsters I was encountering. Feedme got killed and Boohyoo turned wild
after I got tired of it and left it. Later on I ran into it again in
the Valley.

Anyway, I finally decided that I'm prepared enough to enter Gehennom.
I was about Exp:21 or so at this point. Went down to the Valley,
cleared it out, got more loot, then made a detour back to main stash
(I had forgotten to bring money for bribing). Started to make my way
down. Gehennom is SO much less frustrating with magic mapping.
Asmodeus was directly below the Valley (which was what reminded me I
forgot to bring money). Bribed him off. Found Juiblex a few levels
down. Didn't even get sick; he teleported next to me, and I MM'd him
to death before he could harm me. Played around with boulders a bit,
but gave up.  There are never enough boulders to make a clear path
through the swamp... at least, not any that doesn't involve covering
practically the entire swamp---too slow for any purposes. So just gave
up and Lev'd across.  Found Baalzebub not long afterwards, and bribed
him off too.  Orcus wasn't too hard, although it was annoying that the
level was no-teleport. Found Vlad not long after at Dlvl:41.

Ran into a few master liches and arch-liches several times during the
journey; but having MR and teleportitis/TC really helped. I hogged the
stairs before they did, and cancellation weakened their attacks
somewhat. Magicbane absorbed almost all the curses, so they did
minimal damage. The only frightening thing was that at one point, an
arch-lich summoned an MMF right in front of me.  Cancelled him, but he
was reaching for my brains regardless. (I don't know if he can
actually suck anything out after being cancelled; my helmet blocked
his attacks, but it was still a very scary thought.) Another amusing
incident involves fighting arch-liches while blindfolded (in order to
see where it ran to). The arch-lich summoned a swarm of monsters at
one point, and then I proceeded to engrave the E word (with blindfold
on). Needless to say, I wrote it incorrectly (and I wondered, why are
they still hitting me?). So I took off the blindfold, only to be
confused by the arch-lich's spell. So a second try failed. Finally,
applied unihorn and got it right the third time.  (Makes me wonder if
I should've just fired MM at them during all this time.) So I wasted 3
charges from the /oFire.  Anyway, I magic-mapped the entire Gehennom,
and found the vibrating square at Dlvl:50.  Engraved the E word and
left the Candelabrum with 7 candles and the Bell, then levelported
back to main stash to prepare for the ascension run.

I spent a few more wishes on magic markers to write needed spellbooks
and more ?oEA, and fireproofed the rest of my attire. Charmed an Angel
to accompany me on the ascension run. Gave Angela a +3 shield of
reflection and a blessed unihorn. She's one stubborn angel, and
refuses to pick up healing pots I left for her. Took me a while to
convince her that her ring mail sucks. I had collected quite a number
of sets of various dragon scales, but she wouldn't wear them until I
wrote another ?oEA to make real dragonmail from it. Then I gave her
the Dragonbane I got from sac'ing but had no use for, and zapped
/oInvis at her. Somehow, zapping /oSpeed doesn't affect her, so I had
to pester her continually for a long time before she decided to pick
up the /oSpeed and zap herself with it. I tried to give her more
equipment but she refuses to use any of it, so I gave up and let her
be. At least she was AC:-21 when I got everything ready for the
ascension run. (In retrospect, I should've just wished for a blessed
figurine of an Archon.) Anyway, I had dipped my large collection of
?oTeleport in unholy water, so I levelported to Dlvl:1 with a sack
containing some cursed ?oGD, K-rations, and most of my gems (the new
ones I got after the BoH accident), left it there with the E-word,
then levelported back to the altar stash. Left the WoW in the stash,
prepared 2 c!oGL for quickly getting out of the Sanctum. Eye'd into
the Valley with Angela, and headed for Rodney's tower.

Got in without too much trouble, cleared out the zoo although Angela
got scared by something and didn't do very much in the way of helping
at first.  At least she did finish off the few surviving dragons with
her Dragonbane after I FoDded the MMF's. Kicked down the doors for
speed (so I can move diagonally), and made my way up to Rodney. Got a
rubber chicken from the zoo, so I hurried a bit to get to Rodney
before the chicken rotted away.  MM'd the krakens to death, and
=oLev'd to Rodney's bedroom. The smart dirty old fool knew to teleport
out over the moat so I wouldn't rubber chicken him, but he couldn't
resist showing off how he can teleport in a no-teleport level, so as
soon as he appeared inside the bedroom again I politely introduced him
to my rubber chicken. And not a minute too soon; a few moves
afterwards the chicken rotted away. Grabbed the book, and headed out
of the tower.

Levelported to Dlvl:50 and teleportitis'd to the vibrating square.
Performed the invocation, climbed down and back up, and then tried to
levelport to the temple side of the Sanctum. Didn't work the first
time, so I climbed back out and tried again.  Worked the second time:
got to the far west side next to temple. Had lots of fun with the
priests of Moloch; Angela was busy whacking dragons and giant ants
while I killed the demilichs and priests. Tried to ring the Bell to
find the secret door but didn't find anything 'cos it was on the other
side; so resorted to walking on the fire traps and searching. (Shoulda
brought my /oSecretDoorDetection...) Burned up a few useless ?oCM in
the process (am I the only one who purposely walks on fire traps just
so dangerous cursed ?oCM would burn up?), and finally found the door
on the east side of the Inner Sanctum. Kicked down the door, and gave
the high priest the Finger.  Magic whistled Angela into the room,
picked up the Amulet, named it, and quaffed the c!oGL. (BIG kudos to
Wes Irby who suggested this idea on RGRN. This sped up my ascension
run a LOT. Thanks!!)

So began my ascension run. Worked my way to the up stairs using the
/oDigging that I've brought along, and made my way up. The mysterious
force only hit me twice, and didn't bring me down too far. Rodney
appeared once or twice, and I gave him the Finger. The Amulet drained
a lot of Pw, it was a good thing I was very fast, so I could drop the
Amulet and FoD him almost always without him attacking me in between.
Got out of Gehennom without too much setback, and made my way back to
the main stash. Angela was a bit injured after the Sanctum and I tried
giving her more stuff, but she refuses, being the stubborn angel she
is. So I just picked up my WoW just in case, and continued my way
back.  Rodney appeared once or twice more, and got FoDded promptly.
Got back to Dlvl:1 and picked up the ascension stuff. Found that the
bag was too heavy, so I just looted it for the gems and scrolls and
left. (In retrospect, I shoulda taken a few more attack wands as
well.)

Plane of Earth was easy; FoDded Rodney as usual while Angela engaged
the minotaur. I had plenty of /oDigging prepared, so after reading the
c?oGD to find the portal, I dig straight to it. Stopped a few times to
drop the Amulet and MM the earth elementals, but decided eventually
that they don't matter enough so I just marched past them. Scaring
them with Magicbane was a good way to get them out of my way. Found a
band of elf-lords around the portal; Angela started hacking at them
while I prepared for the Plane of Air.

Unfortunately, I prepared everything BUT =oLev. Sighhh... so I had to
pull it out of the BoH and wear it while letting the air elementals
approach. Fortunately I was able to avoid most of them. Got caught in
3 or 4 of them, and /oDeath'd them. Read another c?oGD to find the
portal, and made a beeline for it. Magic-whistled Angela in to make
sure she isn't left behind.

Plane of Fire was annoying. c?oGD turned up way too many $'s, and I
had no way of telling which ones were fire traps and which one is the
portal except by visiting each and every one. Had to circle the Plane
twice to find the portal. In the meantime, Angela got burned badly by
the fire elementals, and I had to magic-whistle her out of trouble
continually (she was hitting a dangerous low of 15 HP). The game
started to get impatient at my lack of progress and sent two Archons
to prod me on. Had to /oTeleport them away just to keep things sane.
Finally, found the portal and magic-whistled Angela in.

Plane of Water was not too bad, except that the constant movement of
the bubbles made it really annoying for killing krakens and eels: I
had to drop the Amulet to prevent using up too much Pw, but as soon as
I dropped it the bubbles shifted and my targets were no longer in line
of fire. Angela got dangerously low on HP (and I really wanted to have
her survive into the Astral Plane) but she REFUSED to pick up the "oLS
I dropped for her. The audacity! I also had no more c?oGD left so it
was anybody's guess where the portal might be. So I spent quite some
time chasing the "oLS which kept floating off into obscure bubbles,
and magic-whistling Angela in to coax her to wear the amulet but to no
avail, and soon the amulet vanished off in some obscure bubble
somewhere while I MM'd the krakens and eels and tried to keep the
water elementals at bay. Discovered that levitating in the Plane of
Water did not prevent me from picking stuff up from the bubbles. Cool.
Rummaged through my stuff to find a !oHeal for Angela but found
nothing (I had used it all up to push my max HP to 400+). And then the
bubble containing the "oLS floated into view. What a coincidence! I
stepped towards it to try to give it to Angela again, but at that
moment, by some weird coincidence, the portal happened to be on the
same square. By another weird coincidence, Angela happened to be
standing next to it, so we both made it to the Astral Plane, but
without the "oLS. (Serves her right, that stubborn angel.)

So I found myself on the west part of the corridor in the Astral Plane
with Angela and a brand new guardian angel. We were almost immediately
attacked by an arch-lich (or master lich), which summoned a horde of
monsters that the two angels had fun dealing with while I MM'd the
lich to death. Found a healing pot on one of the monsters and gave it
to Angela. FINALLY she took it (she was almost down to the single
digits in HP) and drank it. Sheesh. Then I proceeded to the west door
and saw that it was Famine. I took out some K-rations into my main
inventory and prepared for battle. It was slow, as two role characters
were in the corridor with us and just being a thorough nuisance in
general.  The priests of Moloch came through the door along with some
non-coaligned angels, and along came Famine. Famine touched me once
but I didn't get hungry, so I killed him off first. Unfortunately, due
to impedance from the insects summoned by the priests, I couldn't
enter the door in time and Famine rose from the dead again. I managed
to kill 'em off before he could touch me, though. Then I worked my way
slowly to the west door. Pw dropped dangerously low. I magic-whistled
in the two angels and ran around the monsters, relying on my -40 AC to
keep me from getting too injured. I got to the outer temple door when
I got surrounded by two hostile angels, and I was starting to get
quite injured. So I waited for an opportune time when there were two
empty squares next to me, and magic-whistled in the two angels. They
killed off some insects and injured one of the angels some, but Angela
got killed (darn her, if she had only taken the "oLS ...), and the
guardian angel fell shortly after. So I was left alone with about 300
HP and dangerously low on Pw. Slowly worked my way through the hordes,
and a demilich summoned TWO MMF's.  Fortunately, managed to FoD both
of them just in time. Pw dropped even lower, and so I was reduced to
using Magicbane to fend the hordes off and carefully picking a few
select targets for the /oDeath. (Didn't know if I had to survive long
enough to make it to the other high altars.)

Finally, I made it to the temple doors, blinded by some spell or
lightning bolt some monster fired at me. I unihorned, and realized
that the monsters were getting scared. Hmmm, good sign. I still had
wizard lock fresh in memory, so I locked the door behind me and fended
off an angry (and scared) priest of Anhur. Went to the altar, found
that it was neutral.  Huzzah!

And so...

